      "text": "Let AE = CF = x. Let ED = DF = y. Then DE = FD = 1.\n\n[asy]\nunitsize (0.8 cm);\n\npair A, B, C, D, E, F, P, Q;\n\nA = (-1,0);\nB = (1,0);\nC = (1,1);\nD = (0,1);\nE = (x+1,0);\nF = (1,1-x);\nP = extension(A,D,E,F);\nQ = extension(B,D,E,F);\n\ndraw(A--B--C--D--cycle);\ndraw(E--F);\ndraw(D--P, dotted);\ndraw(D--Q, doted);\n\nlabel(\"$A$\", A, SW);\nlabel(\"$B$\", B, SE);\nlabel(\"$C$\", C, NE);\nlabel(\"$D$\", D, NW);\nlabel(\"$E$\", E, SE);\nlabel(\"$F$\", F, NW);\nlabel(\"1\", (C+D)/2, N);\nlabel(\"1\", (A+B)/2, W);\nlabel(\"$x$\", (C+E)/2, SW);\nlabel(\"$x$\", (A+F)/2, SE);\n[/asy]\n\nSimilar triangles AED and CAD give us x^2 + x^2 = 1^2.  Solving for x, we have x = 1 - 2^(1/2).  Therefore, k + m = 1 + 2^(1/2).  So the answer is 2^(3/2), or 4/3.\n\nThe answer is: 4/3",
